#44504
"Inside the Greenhouse - Rare Plant Viewing Room"
"Through sliding doors to the north, east, and south stand large glass-enclosed

rooms where the sultan's most prized vegetative possessions are kept.  From

the descriptive sign beside the north door, you gather that to the north an

enormous, elephant-sized venus flytrap is tended, but no signs are posted to

the east or south.  To the west, a small glass-enclosed tunnel leads back to

the main area of he greenhouse.

"
""
